// TODCameraResend.asi - Total Overdose <-> RTX Remix compatibility shim.
//
// This is a D3D9 vtable-hook layer loaded as an ASI plugin. It does not modify
// TOD.exe; it intercepts the device the game creates and reshapes a few things
// RTX Remix needs in order to raytrace the game. There are four cooperating
// subsystems:
//
//   1. Camera resend (ResendCameraForDraw): TOD only resubmits D3DTS_VIEW when
//      the camera changes. Remix needs valid view/projection state at the draws
//      it raytraces, so cached non-identity view/projection are resent before
//      fixed-function indexed world draws. Identity-view and pre-transformed
//      (RHW) draws are skipped so 2D/overlay passes are left alone.
//
//   2. Render-target redirect (Hook_SetRenderTarget / RT-composite skips): TOD
//      renders the 3D scene into offscreen color render-target textures and then
//      composites them to the backbuffer with pre-transformed fullscreen quads.
//      Remix cannot raytrace that, so full-screen scene RTs are redirected to the
//      primary backbuffer and the RT-texture composites are dropped.
//
//   3. Managed texture shadowing (GetOrCreateDefaultTextureCopy): Remix does not
//      compute an image hash for D3DPOOL_MANAGED textures bound directly, so it
//      skips those drawcalls ("Texture 0 without valid hash"). Each supported
//      managed texture gets a SYSTEMMEM->DEFAULT shadow uploaded via
//      UpdateTexture and the DEFAULT copy is bound at draw time. A conservative
//      draw-time policy (ShouldShadowTextureForDraw) decides when to substitute,
//      to avoid corrupting masks/lightmaps/video.
//
//   4. Candidate discovery (LogTextureCandidateForDraw): optional diagnostic
//      scaffolding, gated by kEnableCandidateDiscovery. Classifies textures by
//      observed draw behavior (ui / hud / video / world / effect), logs a TSV
//      and DDS dumps so real atlas hashes can be identified offline and placed
//      in the Remix config (rtx.uiTextures for UI/HUD, rtx.hideInstanceTextures
//      for broken world LOD). No game content is hardcoded here, and the whole
//      subsystem compiles out when the toggle is false.
//
// All shared counters use Interlocked* so the worker-thread setup and the render
// thread do not race. Diagnostic logging is rate-limited (first N + every Nth).

#define WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN
#include <windows.h>
#include <d3d9.h>
#include <stdarg.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>

#define XXH_INLINE_ALL
#include "../../third_party/dxvk-remix/src/util/xxHash/xxhash.h"

namespace {

